    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster carries significant momentum into today\u2019s slate, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (70.33) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94). **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier offensive engine, drawing a favorable matchup against Sproat; his ability to neutralize right-handed pitching while maintaining an elite power-speed profile makes him a lock. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** enjoys a premium hitting environment against M. Keller, with his strong xwOBA of .378 serving as a floor-raiser for our RBI projections. **Gunnar Henderson** (64.90) provides the most intriguing tactical profile; while the platoon disadvantage against F. Valdez tempers his outlook, his 100% stolen base potential against a slow-delivering lefty keeps his daily ceiling among the highest on the squad. **Jackson Merrill** (61.40) rounds out our top-tier plays, benefitting from a substantial dynamic platoon boost against Medina that helps offset a slightly tougher park factor.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, primarily focused on preserving game caps while navigating a few lingering lineup uncertainties. **Nolan Schanuel** (53.06) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, narrowly falling short of the output projected for **Liam Hicks** (53.47). While **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s projected #3 spot in the order is enticing, the model favored **Liam Hicks**\u2019s leadoff deployment and dynamic platoon advantage against R. Scott. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, as their absence necessitates a heavy reliance on utility depth like **Nasim Nunez** (57.85), who earns the start today thanks to a significant SP skill advantage against M. P\u00e9rez. We remain cautious regarding **Coby Mayo** (54.35) and **Gage Workman** (42.73), both of whom are confirmed lineup pending; should official reports move them lower than the 8-hole, we will pivot to available bench depth such as **Josh Jung** (44.05) to ensure maximum efficiency.",
